**For question 2.37:**

Given diameter of a zinc atom:

\[
2.6\ \text{Å}
\]

Since \(1\ \text{Å}=100\ \text{pm}\),

\[
\text{Diameter}=2.6\times100=260\ \text{pm}
\]

### (a) Radius

\[
\text{Radius}=\frac{\text{diameter}}{2}
=\frac{260}{2}
=\boxed{130\ \text{pm}}
\]

### (b) Number of atoms in a \(1.6\ \text{cm}\) line

Convert the diameter and length to the same unit:

\[
2.6\ \text{Å}=2.6\times10^{-8}\ \text{cm}
\]

The number of atoms is:

\[
N=\frac{1.6\ \text{cm}}{2.6\times10^{-8}\ \text{cm}}
\approx 6.2\times10^{7}
\]

Therefore, the answers are:

\[
\boxed{\text{(a) }130\ \text{pm}}
\]

\[
\boxed{\text{(b) }6.2\times10^{7}\text{ atoms}}
\]

**I can help with one problem at a time. If you'd like help with another question from this sheet, just let me know which one!**

